SQLite for OpenVMS (vms-sqlite) - news
======================================

3.54.1-vms1 (2026-10)

  First kit. SQLite 3.54.1 for OpenVMS x86-64, built with VSI clang (LP64):
  - the sqlite3 shell, the object library LIBSQLITE3.OLB, the shareable
    image SQLITE3$SHR.EXE and the headers;
  - an OpenVMS file layer (VFS) of its own: $QIO block I/O and locks on a
    <database>-lock file, so that several processes, and accounts in
    different UIC groups, can share one database safely;
  - rollback journals only (no WAL), no loadable extensions; FTS5, R*Tree,
    JSON and the math functions built in.
  Tested with SQLite's mptest, a writer stopped at random moments, several
  writer processes, a cross-group test, a SQL corpus compared with SQLite
  on Linux, and PHP for OpenVMS (8.5.12-vms2) running a phpBB board.
